Z||000000||Formula 18||01-21-2001||12:15 AM||||I have an 88 formula and lately it has had some weird problems. <P>#1 My temp gauge bounces all around when you start up the car then stays at the coldest temp no matter how hot the engine gets.  Any ideas?  I know the kid that had the car before me put in a switch the turns the fan on HIGH could this be the problem.  (I think the switch just completes the circuit, ground maybe)<P>#2 My decklid release doesn't do anything when the car isn't running key in or not then when it is running just makes a funny buzzing sound when I push it and if I hold it there....  The interior lights come on.<P>#3 More interior light problems.  The overhead lights are very dim.  Not enough to light to see anything.  The buttons that on the overhead panel make them come on but only if the dimmer switch isn't on.  When the dimmer switch is on the overhead light go off and the side light under the dash come on.  When I open the door the they switch then the overhead light stay on until I hit the brake pedal... this on totally has me confused. <P><BR>Any help would be great.  I am hoping that it is the CURTSY fuse.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-21-2001||11:58 AM||||check the fuses yet? There are multiple fuses involved with interior lighting. "Bat" and "ctsy/lid" must both be good if you have the lights under the dash.<P>check the trunk relay under the dash next.<P>the temp gauge or the sender or the sender wiring could be messed up. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-21-2001).]||||reg||1
